  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam in collaboration with African Economic Research Consortium (AERC) are implementing a collaborative research and policy outreach on the gendered impact of COVID 19 on livelihoods in Africa. The objective of this project is to conduct high quality policy research using novel and innovative approaches, that can shed light on the gendered impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on livelihoods in selected African countries including Kenya, Ethiopia, South Africa, Zambia, and Nigeria. The research takes special emphasis on vulnerable groups who bear the brunt disproportionately, economically, physiologically, and emotionally.

The objective of this Project isto conduct high quality policy research using novel and innovative approaches, including data collection methods that can shed light on the gendered impact of the COVID-19 pandemic on livelihoods in selected African countries with special emphasis on vulnerable groups who bear the brunt disproportionately, economically, physiologically and emotionally.

The project aims to:
&#xf0a7; Evaluate short-medium and long-term macroeconomic consequences of the pandemic on African economies, including the impact on food insecurity, malnutrition and hunger;
&#xf0a7; Examine gendered socio-economic impacts of the pandemic in order to inform, inspire and influence gender transformative policy responses that can benefit larger swathes of the population &#x2013; in particular, women, vulnerable communities and gender diverse people;
&#xf0a7; Use the evidence to build the capacity of researchers and institutions in target countries for longer term, sustainable policy changes that address root causes of the pandemic&#x2019;s unequal impact, including gender inequality; and,
&#xf0a7; Build a network of stakeholders (policy, research, and practice institutions and individuals) that can continue to track the pandemic&#x2019;s impacts and design and advocate for practical, gender-transformative solutions, for building back better post-COVID.

The project targets 6 case studies and continuous policy engagement to be undertaken in Sub-Saharan Africa (SSA). Outputs to be produced under each project component over a two-year period are 6 publications in refereed journals or chapters in book volumes published by leading publishers. The project will also yield enhanced technical skills on impact analysis and feminist advocacy for Africa-based policy analysts and advisors.</narrative>
  </description>
